---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Icons from "../../components/Icons.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Lama Temple vs Temple of Heaven: Which Should You Visit?" description="Lama Temple or Temple of Heaven? Compare the two spiritual landmarks — atmosphere, architecture, rituals, and time needed. Honest verdict on which one fits your Beijing itinerary.">
  <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: "Compare", href: "/#compare-guides" }, { label: "Lama Temple vs Temple of Heaven" }]} />
  <div class="relative py-24 md:py-32 overflow-hidden -mt-[68px]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-cover bg-center" style="background-image:url('/images/attractions/lama-temple.webp')"></div>
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[#0a3b36]/88"></div>
    <div class="relative z-10 mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 text-center">
      <span class="tag tag-glass mb-4">Compare & Decide</span>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight text-white md:text-5xl">Lama Temple vs Temple of Heaven</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 mx-auto max-w-2xl text-lg text-white/80">Two of Beijing's most celebrated temples — one for living faith, one for imperial ritual.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-12 pb-6">
    <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-[#0f766e] pl-5 py-2 rounded-r bg-[#ccfbf1]/30">
      <p class="text-base text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The short answer:</strong> Choose the <strong>Lama Temple</strong> for atmosphere — it is a working Tibetan Buddhist temple where incense, chanting, and the 18-meter sandalwood Buddha make for a moving, compact visit. Choose the <strong>Temple of Heaven</strong> for iconic architecture and the quintessential Beijing park experience — the blue-roofed Hall of Prayer is the city's symbol, and the dawn tai chi scene is unforgettable. They are not really competitors; the Temple of Heaven is a half-day, the Lama Temple a 90-minute stop.</p>
    </blockquote>
  </div>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Side-by-Side Comparison</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Feature</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Lama Temple</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Temple of Heaven</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">What it is</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Working Tibetan Buddhist lamasery</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Imperial ritual park & monument</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Ticket</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 25 (includes incense)</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">CNY 15 combined through-ticket</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Time needed</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">60-90 minutes</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">2-3 hours</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Atmosphere</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Incense, chanting, active worshippers</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Grand monument + lively local park</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Centerpiece</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">18m sandalwood Maitreya Buddha</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">UNESCO</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">No</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Yes</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Local life</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Worshippers & lamas</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Tai chi, opera, kites in the park</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Pair with</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Nanluoguxiang, Guijie food street</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Hongqiao Market, Qianmen</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Subway</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Yonghegong (Line 2/5), Exit C</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Tiantan Dongmen (Line 5), Exit A</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">The Core Difference</h2>
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">The Lama Temple is faith in action</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">This is not a preserved monument — it is a functioning lamasery where monks live and pray, worshippers light incense, and the courtyards fill with smoke and devotion. The 18-meter Maitreya Buddha carved from a single sandalwood tree is the single most extraordinary object on this page, and the experience is intimate: five halls on one axis, incense hanging in the light, Tibetan Buddhist art in every courtyard. It is the closest Beijing gets to stepping into a living religious tradition.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#d5d0c4]/40 p-6 shadow-sm">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-2">The Temple of Heaven is ritual made monumental</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed">The Temple of Heaven is where emperors performed the annual prayer for a good harvest — and the architecture itself is the experience. The circular Hall of Prayer, square park wall, Echo Wall's acoustics, and the numerology woven into every beam are a masterpiece of imperial design. It is also the park where Beijing's morning rituals play out: hundreds of locals practicing tai chi, singing opera, and flying kites. You get a UNESCO monument and the city's living culture in one ticket.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Which One Is Right for You?</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="heart" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Want the most atmospheric religious site?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Lama Temple. Incense, chanting, and the towering Buddha make it the most moving — and it is compact enough to slot anywhere in a day.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="star" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Want the iconic Beijing photo?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Temple of Heaven. The blue-roofed Hall of Prayer is the architectural symbol of Beijing, and its marble terraces are a photographer's dream.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="clock" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Only have 90 minutes?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Lama Temple. Five halls on one axis can be done meaningfully in an hour. The Temple of Heaven deserves 2-3 hours, especially if you arrive for the dawn rituals.</p></div></div>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3"><Icons name="users" size={20} class="text-[#0f766e] mt-0.5 shrink-0" /><div><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">Traveling with kids?</strong><p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] mt-1">Temple of Heaven — the Echo Wall and Circular Mound acoustics fascinate children, and the vast park is perfect for running around. The Lama Temple's devotion is better appreciated by adults.</p></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-8 border-t border-[#edeae3] pt-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Our Verdict by Traveler Type</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto border border-[#d5d0c4] rounded-xl">
      <table class="w-full text-sm">
        <thead class="bg-[#f8f7f4] text-[#5c5a4c] uppercase text-xs tracking-wider">
          <tr><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">If you are...</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Pick</th><th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-left">Why</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Short on time</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Lama Temple</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Complete in 90 minutes</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Want THE Beijing photo</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Temple of Heaven</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Iconic Hall of Prayer</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">Seeking atmosphere</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Lama Temple</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Living faith, incense, Buddha</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">With kids</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Temple of Heaven</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Echo Wall + open park</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-[#edeae3]"><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">History buff</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Temple of Heaven</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Imperial cosmology in architecture</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-[#1c1a16]">UNESCO collector</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#0f766e] font-semibold">Temple of Heaven</td><td class="px-4 py-3 text-[#5c5a4c]">Listed World Heritage site</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1c1a16] mb-4">Can You Do Both?</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed mb-4">Absolutely — they are actually easy to pair on one day. The Temple of Heaven shines as a morning visit (arrive for the dawn tai chi, then the monuments), and the Lama Temple works perfectly as a late-afternoon stop on the way to Guijie for dinner. Both sit on Line 5, so the metro does most of the work. Together they cover both halves of Beijing's spiritual life: the imperial ritual of the past and the living faith of the present.</p>
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#fef3c7] border border-[#d4a373]/30 p-6">
      <p class="text-sm text-[#5c5a4c] leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-[#1c1a16]">The honest bottom line:</strong> if you must choose one, the Temple of Heaven is the more important site — it is the icon and the UNESCO-listed monument, and its park is Beijing at its most alive. But the Lama Temple is the more moving experience, and at 90 minutes it is the easier one to fit in. Most visitors should find room for both.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
